# Story 4: Configuring Rysh (50s)
# Hook: One TOML file controls everything -- and every setting has an env-var override.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-004-configuring-rysh.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Rysh reads one TOML config file -- and every setting also has an environment-variable override.

[00:05.0 --> 00:13.0]
The config lives at ~/.config/rysh/rysh.config, or rysh.config in your current directory.

[00:13.0 --> 00:24.0]
The provider section sets your model and API key. Set api_key to call the Anthropic API directly -- otherwise Rysh falls back to the claude CLI.

[00:24.0 --> 00:34.0]
The ui section controls your shell and how many tabs and panes open on a fresh start.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
The upstream section enables remote sharing -- point it at a rysh-server and drop in an API key.

[00:42.0 --> 00:50.0]
Every value has an env override. Just prefix your launch -- here, RYSH_API_KEY -- and rysh picks it up.

